---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How TubWise collects, uses, and shares information when you visit gettubwise.com."
  path="/privacy"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <p class="text-sm text-ink-subtle">Effective date: August 2, 2026</p>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who operates TubWise</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise operates the website at{' '}
    <a href="https://gettubwise.com">https://gettubwise.com</a> from Florida. We publish
    educational guides and tools for hot tub owners. This Privacy Policy explains what
    information may be collected when you use the site and how that information is
    handled.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>

  <h3 id="automatic">Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Like most websites, TubWise is served through a hosting provider. When you visit the
    site, standard technical information is typically processed in server or CDN logs.
    That can include your IP address, browser type, device or operating-system
    information, referring URL, pages requested, and the date and time of the request.
  </p>
  <p>
    TubWise also uses <strong>Vercel Web Analytics</strong>, a privacy-focused traffic
    measurement tool provided by Vercel (the same company that hosts the site). The
    analytics script records anonymous, aggregated page-view data such as the page URL,
    referrer, approximate geolocation (for example, country or city), device type, and
    browser or operating-system details. According to Vercel, Web Analytics does not use
    third-party cookies for visitor identification and does not collect personal
    identifiers meant to track people across unrelated websites. TubWise does not run
    Google Analytics, advertising pixels, error-logging, or other third-party analytics
    or advertising scripts on the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you use site search, your query may appear in the page URL (for example,{' '}
    <code>/search?q=...</code>). Hosting logs and analytics page-view data may reflect
    that full request URL.
  </p>

  <h3 id="voluntary">Information you provide voluntarily</h3>
  <p>
    TubWise does not offer accounts, newsletters, comment systems, payments, or an
    on-site contact form. If you email us at{' '}
    <a href="mailto:hello@gettubwise.com">hello@gettubwise.com</a>, you choose what to
    include in that message. That typically includes your email address and any name,
    spa details, or other information you write. We use that information to respond to
    your message and to keep ordinary correspondence records.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies-and-similar">Cookies, local storage, and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise does not set advertising cookies, and the site code does not use browser
    local storage or session storage for tracking. Vercel Web Analytics is designed to
    measure traffic without third-party cookies; visitor sessions are identified using
    a hash derived from the request rather than a persistent cookie. Search works in
    your browser by loading a static search index from the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your browser may still store ordinary temporary data needed to display pages, and
    third-party services that the site loads may use their own technologies, as
    described below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="why-we-process">Why information is processed</h2>
  <p>Information described in this policy is processed to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Operate, secure, and deliver the website</li>
    <li>Understand aggregated site traffic and which pages are used</li>
    <li>Respond to messages you send</li>
    <li>Understand and fix technical issues when they appear in hosting logs</li>
    <li>Maintain ordinary business and legal records related to the site</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="service-providers">Service providers that may receive information</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise uses service providers to run the site. Based on the current site
    configuration and production hosting headers, those providers include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Vercel</strong>, which hosts and delivers the static site, may process
      standard request logs and related infrastructure data, and provides Vercel Web
      Analytics used to measure anonymous, aggregated page views
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Fonts</strong> (fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com), which
      the site loads to display fonts; Google may receive your IP address and browser
      information when font files are requested
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email providers</strong>, if you send email to TubWise, because your
      message travels through ordinary email systems
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers process information on TubWise&apos;s behalf or as part of delivering
    their services. TubWise does not currently use advertising networks, chat widgets,
    payment processors, or account systems, and it does not use separate analytics
    platforms other than Vercel Web Analytics.
  </p>

  <h2 id="selling-and-sharing">Selling and sharing of personal information</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise does not sell personal information, and it does not share personal
    information with third parties for targeted advertising. Using hosting, font
    delivery, and email infrastructure is not the same as selling information or running
    advertising profiles.
  </p>
  <p>
    TubWise may disclose information if required by law, to respond to a valid legal
    process, or to protect the security and integrity of the site and its users.
  </p>

  <h2 id="affiliate-tracking">Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise maintains an <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a> page.
    The site does not currently include live affiliate links or affiliate tracking
    scripts. If affiliate links are added later and you follow one, the affiliate partner
    or network may collect information about that click under its own privacy practices,
    which can include cookies or referral identifiers needed to attribute a purchase. We
    do not control those third-party practices.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long information is kept</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise does not publish fixed retention calendars for every data type. In practice:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Hosting and CDN logs are retained according to the hosting provider&apos;s practices
      and TubWise&apos;s need to operate and secure the site
    </li>
    <li>
      Vercel Web Analytics visitor-session identifiers are discarded after 24 hours per
      Vercel&apos;s product practices; aggregated analytics are retained according to
      Vercel&apos;s practices for the service
    </li>
    <li>
      Email correspondence is kept as long as needed to respond and for ordinary business
      records, then deleted or archived when it is no longer needed
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise takes reasonable steps to protect the site and correspondence, including
    serving pages over HTTPS through its hosting provider. No method of transmission or
    storage is completely secure, and TubWise cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2 id="external-links">External links</h2>
  <p>
    Guides on TubWise often link to manufacturer manuals, public-health pages, and other
    third-party websites. Those sites have their own privacy practices. TubWise is not
    responsible for the content or privacy practices of external sites.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children&apos;s privacy</h2>
  <p>
    TubWise is intended for a general audience of hot tub owners and is not directed to
    children under 13. TubWise does not knowingly collect personal information from
    children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided personal information,
    contact TubWise using the details below and the information will be deleted when
    reasonably possible.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Privacy requests and consumer rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, applicable law may give you rights to request access to,
    correction of, or deletion of personal information you provided, or to ask questions
    about how it is handled. TubWise will review privacy requests in good faith and respond
    as required by applicable law.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy describes TubWise&apos;s practices. It is not a claim that TubWise is
    certified under, or formally assessed against, any specific privacy statute.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-to-contact">How to submit a privacy request</h2>
  <p>
    To ask a privacy-related question or submit a request, email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:hello@gettubwise.com">hello@gettubwise.com</a>. Please include enough
    detail for us to understand and verify your request. Do not send emergency repair or
    safety-critical issues by email; contact a qualified professional instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this Privacy Policy changes, TubWise will update this page and revise the effective
    date at the top. Continued use of the site after an update means the revised policy
    applies to later visits, except where a different notice is required by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="related">Related pages</h2>
  <p>
    See also the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>, <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>,
    and <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
